4. Maximal-gate nine-speed fan
   A local endpoint-cover proof by largest speed fails in a structured
   way: a dyadic speed v has a nine-speed lower fan that covers all
   2v endpoints.  The normalized fan is stable.
   v     gcd(fan) normalized fan                  covered gains
   16    1        (8, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15)    32/32   16,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2
   32    1        (16, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15)   64/64   32,4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4
   64    2        (16, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15)  128/128  64,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8
   128   4        (16, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15)  256/256  128,16,16,16,16,16,16,16,16
   256   8        (16, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15)  512/512  256,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32
   512   16       (16, 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15) 1024/1024 512,64,64,64,64,64,64,64,64
   New proof target: if a maximal branch closes by this fan, the fan is
   imprimitive at scale gcd=v/32.  The six remaining speeds must break
   that gcd and simultaneously protect the fan's descendant endpoints.

