6. Synthesis / next proof attempt
   A counterexample at n=16 must now pass three gates at once:
   (i) contain a 16-gate by the unit-skeleton lemma;
   (ii) have no antipodal pair gap in E OR (O AND tau O);
   (iii) if a maximal dyadic branch uses the nine-speed fan, the six
   non-fan speeds must break the fan gcd without creating private debt.
   The wild idea that survived this pass is to prove incompatibility
   between (ii) and (iii).  Odd double-coverage wants two odd lanes on
   every pair not already covered by evens; the maximal fan wants a
   scaled odd residue fan plus a half-gate.  Those demands point in
   opposite quotient directions once primitivity is imposed.
